  "title": "🤖 Week 29: Game AI",
  "date": "2025-07-10T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "🤖 Week 29: Game AI\n\nThis week, I finally finished Unity's AI course. The crowd simulation and Goal Driven Behavior sections were really fun and insightful!\n\nLearning Agents in UE5\n\nAfter Unity, I explored Unreal Engine’s Learning Agents.\n\nUsing Blueprints can be a bit tedious… I still prefer C++ for more control 😅.\n\nML-Agents in Unity\n\nML-Agents is a Unity package that makes training AI agents easier.\n\nHighly recommend checking out Code Monkey’s tutorials:\n\nHow to use Machine Learning AI in Unity! (ML-Agents)\n\nTeach your AI! Imitation Learning with Unity ML-Agents!\n\nIt’s amazing to see agents learn and adapt — makes game worlds feel alive! 🚀",
